text": "The ICJ is headquartered in The Hague, where it conducts its hearings and deliberations."}, {"sourceSlug": "united-nations-general-assembly", "sourceName": "United Nations General Assembly", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "statute-of-the-international-court-of-justice", "targetName": "Statute of the International Court of Justice", "context": "The UN General Assembly plays a key role in referring legal questions to the ICJ for advisory opinions."}], "places": [{"name": "San Francisco, United States", "role": "Creation Site"}, {"name": "The Hague, Netherlands", "role": "Headquarters"}, {"name": "New York City, United States", "role": "UN General Assembly Location"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Statute of the International Court of Justice", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "statute-of-the-international-court-of-justice"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2066389", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statute_of_the_International_Court_of_Justice"], "tags": ["treaty", "International Treaties & Conventions", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Key lasting impacts include: Shaped diplomatic relations and territorial boundaries. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "The ICJ has played a pivotal role in shaping international law and resolving disputes between nations, influencing treaties and international relations since 1945.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-30T13:11:54Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30545273640", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "United nations statute Created by International Court of Justice.", "newValue": "The Statute of the International Court of Justice (ICJ), adopted on April 29, 1945, during the United Nations Conference on International Organization in San Francisco, serves as the foundational legal document establishing the ICJ's framework and operational guidelines. The ICJ, located in The Hague, Netherlands, is the principal judicial organ of the United Nations and plays a crucial role in resolving disputes between states and providing advisory opinions on international legal issues. The creation of the ICJ marked a significant step in the evolution of international law and diplomacy, aiming to promote peace and security after the catastrophic impacts of World War II.

The Statute outlines the jurisdiction, procedures, and functions of the Court, which hears cases brought by states and issues advisory opinions on legal questions referred to it by the UN General Assembly and Security Council. With 15 judges elected for nine-year terms, the Court's deliberations are based on principles of justice and international law, drawing upon treaties, customary law, and judicial decisions. Its first case was adjudicated in 1947, setting precedents for future international legal proceedings and enhancing the role of the judiciary in global governance.

The legacy of the Statute is profound, as it has established a framework that has been referenced in numerous international treaties and legal instruments, fostering a culture of compliance with international law among nations. The ICJ's decisions have influenced various global conflicts, such as the territorial disputes in the South China Sea and the legality of the use of force, thus shaping the international legal landscape. This legal institution has also inspired the creation of other international courts and tribunals, contributing to a more structured approach to international dispute resolution and human rights enforcement."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-30T13:11:54Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30545273640", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Diplomatic negotiation and conflict resolution"], "newValue": ["The devastation of World War II prompted the need for a permanent judicial body to promote peace and resolve disputes.", "The establishment of the United Nations created a framework for international cooperation and legal adjudication.", "Pre-existing international legal frameworks, such as the Permanent Court of International Justice, influenced the creation of the ICJ's Statute."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-30T13:11:54Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30545273640", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Shaped diplomatic relations and territorial boundaries"], "newValue": ["The ICJ has adjudicated over 170 cases since its establishment, significantly impacting international relations and legal norms.", "Its advisory opinions have guided the actions of UN member states and influenced international treaties and agreements.", "The establishment of the ICJ has led to the proliferation of international courts, enhancing global governance and accountability."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-30T13:11:54Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30545273640", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "statute-of-the-internationa